###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table 2 is read as rows of energy then force per molecule and columns sGDML, SchNet, DimeNet; only the DimeNet column is encoded (the other two are literature values). The summary row 'std. MAE (%)' (2.49 energy, 1.10 forces) is not encoded.
# - The MD17 reference level (DFT) and data-set sizes beyond the 1000 training samples are not restated, so no reference calculation is attached. numRadialBasis = 6 is N_RBF = N_SRBF and numAngularBasis = 7 is N_SHBF; N_bilinear = 8 is not encoded. The hyperparameters were tuned on QM9 and are stated once for the whole model.
# - QM9 (Table 1: twelve molecular properties for 130k equilibrium molecules) is a property-prediction benchmark and is not encoded; nor is the 50,000-sample benzene result quoted in the text (0.035 kcal/mol energy MAE, or 0.07 kcal/mol and 0.17 kcal/mol/A depending on the force weight).
# - The registry origin of entity:DimeNet is now this file. The manifest classes the paper as 'Application/model instance'; it introduces the method.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
